text:
Mia Wang: Quick check  compact nav + deep link behavior: show a tiny breadcrumb or rely only on header workspace? We saw short links drop workspace filter sometimes :thinking_face:
Omar Khan: Tiny breadcrumb keeps landing context. If we hide it, header must expose workspace and be keyboard-focusable. Also prefer a single canonical route so hydration is predictable.
Jamie Lee: Two URL shapes today: `/w/:ws/...` and `/models/:id?ws=`. Proposal: canonicalize to `/w/:ws/...` and client-rewrite the query form on first load. Emit an analytic event when we rewrite.
Nora Patel: A11y nits: breadcrumb must be inside a `nav[aria-label]`, active crumb gets `aria-current=\"page\"`, truncated crumbs need `aria-label` with full text. Mobile: tap opens an action sheet (role=dialog) with "Open parent workspace" and "Copy link".
Mia Wang: UX: condensed crumb = single line, 14px, ellipsize. On widths <320px hide workspace and reveal it in the sheet. Tooltips desktop-only.
ux-scout: Spec link added: https://redwood.design/ux/nav-compact-paths  includes canary plan and a11y checklist.
Jamie Lee: Small hydrate snippet we can add to RFC:
```
// on boot
if (location.search.includes('ws=') && location.pathname.startsWith('/models/')) {
  const p = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
  const ws = p.get('ws');
  const id = location.pathname.split('/').pop();
  history.replaceState({}, '', `/w/${ws}/models/${id}` + location.search);
  telemetry.track('migrate_query_ws');
}
```
Omar Khan: Also migrate old `#panel=` hashes -> `?panel=` and emit `legacy_hash_migrated`. Add `?preserveNav=0|1` for embed cases.
Mia Wang: I'll update mocks and post frames. Tagging @Nora for final a11y pass. Thanks!
